│ patch_description        │ The greedy assignment places each model on the GPU minimizing KVPR at the time, but it    │
│                          │ can be trapped in poor local choices. Adding a cheap local-search refinement pass after   │
│                          │ the greedy step—repeatedly moving or swapping models if it reduces the maximum KVPR       │
│                          │ across GPUs—typically yields a noticeably lower max KVPR with negligible runtime, since   │
│                          │ test instances are small. The objective for a move/swap is the resulting maximum KVPR     │
│                          │ over all GPUs, which directly matches the metric being minimized.                         │
