│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kvpr_minmax_greedy_plus_refinement                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current greedy assigns each model to the GPU with the lowest resulting KVPR, but it   │
│                          │ ignores the global objective: minimizing the maximum KVPR across GPUs. Two improvements:  │
│                          │ (1) when choosing a GPU, consider the resulting global max KVPR (i.e., prefer a GPU whose │
│                          │ new KVPR stays below the current max if possible, otherwise pick the one minimizing the   │
│                          │ new KVPR) — equivalently always pick the GPU minimizing the resulting KVPR but never      │
│                          │ exceed the current max unnecessarily; (2) add a lightweight post-placement local search   │
│                          │ that repeatedly moves a model from the worst-KVPR GPU to another GPU whenever it strictly │
│                          │ lowers the global maximum KVPR, which fixes greedy mistakes. This keeps runtime tiny      │
│                          │ while reducing the peak KVPR.                                                             │
