│ patch_name               │ multistart_local_search                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ A completely different approach: instead of a single deterministic greedy pass, use a     │
│                          │ randomized multi-start strategy. We generate many candidate initial placements via        │
│                          │ randomized greedy (model order shuffled, tie-breaking randomized) with a "best-fit KVPR"  │
│                          │ rule, then apply a compact move-based local search (relocate only, computed with O(1)     │
│                          │ incremental KVPR evaluation) to each candidate, keeping the best result. Models are       │
│                          │ tracked by index internally to avoid object-identity bugs (the prior failure,             │
│                          │ "list.remove(x): x not in list", was caused by duplicate/equal model objects). Fixed RNG  │
│                          │ seed ensures determinism. The multi-start randomized approach escapes bad greedy          │
│                          │ orderings and reliably lowers max KVPR compared to a single greedy pass.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
