│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_moves_and_stronger_perturbation                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Two targeted improvements: (1) The local-search `refine` only considers moving a model    │
│                          │ off the hottest GPU; when all moves fail, it can still often improve via a swap between   │
│                          │ the hottest GPU and another GPU (exchanging models with different load/size can lower the │
│                          │ hot KVPR when no model alone fits elsewhere). I add a swap phase to `refine`. (2) The ILS │
│                          │ perturbation currently relocates a single random model; a stronger perturbation (1–3      │
│                          │ random relocations) helps escape local optima that single moves cannot, and since runtime │
│                          │ is essentially free (0.01s), more aggressive restarts are affordable. Both changes keep   │
│                          │ determinism via the fixed RNG seed.                                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
