│ patch_name               │ multistart_ils_placement                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Combine the best greedy variant (minimize post-placement KVPR, tie-break by more          │
│                          │ remaining memory) with a candidate-pool approach: build several diverse greedy initial    │
│                          │ solutions (different sort orders and tie-breaking rules), run local search (move + swap + │
│                          │ 3-cycle) from each candidate, and keep the best result. This hedges against a single      │
│                          │ greedy ordering landing in a poor local basin, as recommended. Runtime is tiny so we can  │
│                          │ afford multiple restarts. Local-search moves are shared via helper functions to keep the  │
│                          │ code compact.                                                                             │
