│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ three_cycle_refinement                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Extends the current greedy + move/swap local search with a third move type: 3-cycle       │
│                          │ rotation of models across the two hottest GPUs. When moves and pairwise swaps fail, try   │
│                          │ relocating model A from the hottest GPU to the second-hottest, model B from the           │
│                          │ second-hottest back to the hottest, plus a third model C rotating from second-hottest to  │
│                          │ hottest (or via a third GPU), accepting only strict improvements guarded by epsilon. This │
│                          │ escapes local optima that 2-model swaps cannot, further minimizing the maximum KVPR while │
│                          │ preserving feasibility (memory-fit checks) and termination (strict-improvement guard).    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
